        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Metalwork",
        "topic": "Metal extraction methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2002",
        "question_text": "<p>The process of extracting iron from its ore using a blast furnace involves the reduction of <b>haematite</b> ($Fe_2O_3$) with which of the following?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In a blast furnace, iron is extracted from haematite ($Fe_2O_3$) by reducing it with carbon monoxide ($CO$), which is produced from the reaction of coke (carbon) with oxygen. The reduction reaction is: $Fe_2O_3 + 3CO \rightarrow 2Fe + 3CO_2$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "23772",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "Hydrogen ($H_2$)",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "41404",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "Carbon monoxide ($CO$)",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "12546",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "Nitrogen ($N_2$)",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "96644",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "Oxygen ($O_2$)",
                "is_correct": false
            }
        ],
        "_page_num": 1,
